{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_019sBugyQKSovjsTLSxw8NsY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty, running as a persistent local web app on this machine (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`, served at `http://localhost:8777` by the NSSM `anchor` service). Grounded claims about what it is and ships:\n\n- **Purpose â€” a GTD-style task/project manager backed by plain markdown.** The source of truth is markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files under `domains/`, plus `CANCELLED.md`/`SAVED_FOR_LATER.md` archives). No database, no sync â€” one folder, plain text. Tasks move through a lifecycle: Active â†’ Done / Cancelled / Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored.\n\n- **Ships two engines over the same data.** `anchor_gui.py` is the primary interface â€” a stdlib-only Python HTTP server that renders the full dashboard and writes markdown directly via `/api/*` endpoints (add/done/edit/capture/cancel/save/restore). `anchor.py` is a CLI mirror of the same logic that also generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Self-tests itself daily.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs at 5 AM (Task Scheduler), parsing every file, booting a throwaway server, exercising every endpoint and task state, and writing `health_reports/YYYY-MM-DD.md`; failures raise a red banner in the dashboard.\n\n- **Its biggest feature is an R&D \"control surface\" â€” a mission-control cockpit for AI trio work.** Each project gets a window that drives the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill trio (research â†’ plan â†’ build). This has been built in four iterations, all merged to master:\n  - **v2:** session model, cached/validated summaries, Grass-Catchers idea lane, deliverable pin/declare, an interactive terminal substrate.\n  - **v3 \"Mission Control\":** real ConPTY terminals (the one declared native dep, `pywinpty`), per-session git-worktree isolation, a stacking window manager, in-place expandable summaries, runnable deliverable previews (always on a free port â‰  8777), and Ghost World Labs branding.\n  - **v4 \"Project Cockpit\":** lane tiles with status lights, inline expanding panels (summary + resizable xterm.js terminal), a single seeded terminal substrate (skill loads/greets exactly once â€” fixing the repeating-prompt bug), a claudeâ†”gemini engine toggle, per-lane doc roles, a cost/tokens/time rollup, grass-idea promotion, and type-aware deliverable launch.\n\n- **Design discipline:** Python stdlib only, with a single declared exception (`pywinpty`, lazy, terminal-only); `distro.py` enforces this by refusing any other native/third-party import in product code. All files stay plain-text and accessible from any CLI tool.\n\nNote: the current branch (`foreman/rnd-v4.1-cockpit`) has uncommitted work in progress beyond the merged v4 baseline."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45330,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"462e16a8-1a12-43f8-875f-6cbafc07dca9","uuid":"df3411a8-9941-4320-954f-8fd980804956","request_id":"req_011Cc1oCZk7oEdvcXpF8YDwp"}
